### Reconciliations and exclusions from findings

The existing design at `feature-assembly-plan.md:35` and `:36` explicitly identifies the Phase A 403-denial and “no verification while throttled” wording conflicts, records the corrected behavior and states operator confirmation at Phase B. They are not counted as unresolved PM requirements. Formal validator approval history remains subject to PR2; this lane did not edit approval records.

No finding requires a feature-assembly-plan.md deliverable: the already-present file was inspected as raw design evidence. Missing future runtime files, completed real-IdP tests, current implementation coverage and feature-action signoffs are not readiness defects by themselves. They belong to the later feature run. The 80% floor is explicitly planned in stories and `STATUS.md:60`.

